#basePath P3_UpstreamBarriers
#include "Header.leaf"

:: AtBarrierSite
@exposed
@cutscene
@trigger    OnLocationChanged
// global:currentThread ensures the correct thread
// global:currentPhase == 3 ensures player is in phase 3
@when       global:currentThread == "NONE", global:currentPhase == 3, location == "BarrierSite"
// Mark start of thread
$set global:currentThread = "P3_UpstreamBarriers"

$call  ClearVisibleLines()

// Lock all location on map
$call SetInThreadLocks()
$call DisableMapButton()
$call SetBackground("bg/barrier-site-bg.png")

{@}   
       It's not really much of a barrier by your standards. Beside it, Robertson looks like they could jump over it. 

{@You}
       Does this really do anything?

{@Robertson}
       I can see why ya'd ask. But yes, it works. A sea lamprey ain't much of a swimmer. Actually, they tend to float to the bottom. 
       So a barrier that's low like this can keep sea lamprey from jumping over. But the rest of the fish go over with no issue. 

{@}
       Just as they're speaking, you see a flash of silvery scales as a Chinook Salmon clears the barrier. 

{@Robertson}
       See what I mean? Easy. 

{@You}
       Are there more of these? They seem to be pretty effective.

{@Robertson}
       Unfortunately not. This is the only one that was built. We could build more, though.
$call GiveEvidenceChip("Evidence-barrier")

{@You}
       We'd need the plans. You wouldn't happen to know where those could be?

{@Robertson}
       I can't say anything about particular plans, but Fish and Wildlife Services originally built this barrier.

{@You}
       I guess I'll go there. Thanks for the lead, Robertson. 

{@Robertson} 
       Any time. 

$call UnlockLocation(FishAndWildlife)
$call SetTravelTime(FishAndWildlife, 1)
$call EnableMapButton()
$call CheckIfOutOfTime()
$call OpenMap()


:: AtFishAndWildlife
@trigger    OnLocationChanged
// global:currentThread ensures the correct thread
// global:currentPhase == 3 ensures player is in phase 3
@when       global:currentThread == "P3_UpstreamBarriers", global:currentPhase == 3, location == "FishAndWildlife"
// Lock all location on map
$call SetInThreadLocks()
$call DisableMapButton()
$call SetBackground("bg/fish-and-wildlife-bg.png")

$call  ClearVisibleLines()


{@}   
       The Fish and Wildlife building sits at the end of a dirt road, as rustic as its name. 
       Surprisingly, it's Paul who comes outside to greet you.  
       
{@Paul}
       Welcome to the Department of Fish and Wildlife Services. How can I help you?

{@You}
       Haha. Very funny. Nice to meet you, too. But I do need your help. 

{@Paul}
       Mm. That's what I thought.

{@You}
       The sass is new. I like it. Anyway, the Corps told me that Fish and Wildlife Services built the old barrier. 
       I was wondering if you still have the plans. 

{@Paul}
       Mm. I'm nothing if not meticulous. 

{@}
       He produces a blueprint and shows it to you. 

{@Paul}
       Mm, it won't be cheap, but it can be done. We all have the know-how of what to do. 

{@You}
       If there's anything this experience has taught me, it's that there is a lot of know-how. It's just a matter of putting things on track. 
       So I'll reach out to you if I ever need a barrier built. 

{@Paul}
       Mm. Yes, I should be able to help. 
$call GiveActionCard("Action-barriers")

{@You}
       Thanks, Paul. 

$if !HasSeen(P3_Pheromones.End) //checks to see if player has already seen ending dialogue
       //does nothing if they have
$else
       {@You}
              I guess you were right, then.

       {@Paul}
              Hmm?

       {@You}
              Earlier, you asked me about what I thought about coming to town. I didn't like how much it'd changed. 
              But the future is a gift. I'm glad I'm here to see it. 

       {@Paul}
              There's no time like the present. 

       {@}
              You can't help but agree. 
$endif
// TODO: Give action card

// skip to end
$goto .End


:: End
@exposed
@tracked

// Mark end of thread
$set global:currentThread = "NONE"

// Go to Phase 2 Continue Hub
$goto P3_Hub.Continue